    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "`invoice_totals` is now implemented in `solution.py` to the spec, and the 16 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`.\n\nIt validates every input listed in the spec and raises `ValueError` on any bad one. Each line's net is the unit price times quantity, reduced by the line discount, then by the stacked 5% bulk discount where it applies. Net and tax are rounded to cents per line with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, so totals are plain sums of the rounded line values. Credit is capped at the gross, and `tax_by_rate` includes only the rates that appear on a line, including 0.\n\nThe tests cover:\n- Empty invoices.\n- The stacked 10% then 5% discount.\n- Bulk discount not applying to books.\n- Per-line rounding.\n- Partial and full credit use.\n- Each error case.\n- The 0 and 100 discount limits.",
